Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the msgpack module
=============================================

The native module and qpp compiler metadata belong to qore-msgpack-module.
HTML documentation and the upstream example test belong to the optional
qore-msgpack-module-doc package. Debhelper creates matching debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment containing the packaged Qore runtime
and libqore-dev, then install the Build-Depends from debian/control. The current
qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages.
Other Debian/Ubuntu releases and architectures need their own qualified SDK
and native build/test run. Cross builds are rejected because qpp and Qore
execute during compilation. The MPack 1.0 amalgamation in extern_libs is compiled privately into this
module, with extensions, compatibility and read/write tracking enabled and
unused Node/Expect APIs disabled. Its MIT notice is included in copyright.
No MPack shared library or headers are installed. This is ludocode/MPack;
the distribution's similarly named libmpack is a different implementation.
No native dependency beyond the standard C/C++ libraries is needed.

The build uses distribution compiler/hardening flags. Native Qore modules
resolve Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. debian/rules derives
a minimum runtime and libqore SONAME package dependency from the installed SDK;
dh_shlibdeps supplies other shared-library dependencies. The runtime package is
not Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native Qore interpreter and
includes shared compiler metadata. There are no AOT user modules or Qore
dependency trailers in this module; ordinary dh_strip is appropriate.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot follows the 1.0.1
release and sorts before a future 1.0.2 release. From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.0.1+git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../msgpack-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-msgpack-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../msgpack-package-work/qore-msgpack-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../msgpack-package-work/qore-msgpack-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../msgpack-package-work
    cp -a debian "../msgpack-package-work/qore-msgpack-module-$version/"
    cd "../msgpack-package-work/qore-msgpack-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a clean directory. With dependencies
preinstalled, build as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen; architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc
package. Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

The upstream suite tests MessagePack and Qore-mode values, extension classes,
packing/unpacking errors, named arguments, timestamps and indirect references.
Installed autopkgtests run the same suite away from the build tree, then use
the installed SDK and metadata to compile a named-argument serialization
round trip. No external service or optional Qore module is needed.

Check source/binary Lintian, detached debug symbols and hardening, installation
without libqore-dev, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall,
and reproducibility from two distinct build directories. Retain the exact source
commit, source/package hashes, dependency versions and logs. Publishing to the
testing PPA is separate from approval for a final general release.
